EDGE {
 "proposal_id": "pe135_parr_rel_04",
 "optional": true,
 "source": "joy_parr",
 "target": "gender",
 "type": "connection",
 "relationship_kind": "contribution",
 "directed": true,
 "relationship": "Disaggregating the sexual division of labour: gender and class compared across workplaces, read beyond Canada (1988–93)",
 "map_label": "Gender and class compared, 1988–93",
 "evidence_note": "In-period, her own words: the CSSH article of 1988 (first-page extract read, p. 511) observes that 'economists and feminist theorists have been interested in sexual divisions as general features of the economic or sex/gender system rather than as boundaries between tasks forged in defined contexts by particular clashes of interest', and that 'most analysts have dealt with gender division as a characteristic of the work force as a whole'. Reviews of The Gender of Breadwinners outside Canada (all read in full): Benson (JAH, 1993, p. 1630) writes that 'few historians have successfully integrated the discussion of these two fundamental relationships' and that 'Parr joins this small but growing group'. On p. 1631 Benson continues: 'Like others influenced by post-structuralist theory, she emphasizes the shifting and multivalent meanings often obscured by dualisms'; Parr 'gives gender and class coordinate roles in her analysis but downplays ethnicity'. Dennis (EcHR, 1991) finds that she 'goes far beyond previous accounts of connections between capitalism and patriarchy' (p. 761) but faults graphs that 'cavalierly use straight lines to connect a handful of isolated observations' (p. 762). Bertaux (JEH, 1992) wants 'a basic quantitative summary of work force data' (p. 240) but concludes that 'the topic of gender and work is not strictly a \"women's issue\"' (p. 241). The book itself is unread here. This records reception in international journals, not adoption. Optional: edge_840 (cdn_women_gender → gender) already links the Canadian field to the international entry.",
 "source_ids": [
  "pe135_parr_cssh_1988",
  "cdnsrc_parr_1990",
  "pe135_parr_benson_1993",
