data/extension-2026/canadian-persons-2026-10-14/valverde/entry-draft.json:154:   "reason": "Not proposed. She criticises class-functionalist and political-economy accounts of welfare: in 1991 'Marxist accounts (and in Canada this chiefly means accounts produced by the political economy school)' and liberal accounts alike (p. 165, snippets; elsewhere her notes cite Panitch, ed., The Canadian State, 1977, and find in Guest's The Emergence of Social Security in Canada 'a liberal framework', p. 170), and in 1992 Fecteau's 'rather functionalist formulation' and 'the pitfalls of marxist functionalism' (p. 222, read). No atlas entry holds the Canadian political-economy position; a critique of marx would generalise a dispute that she frames inside the left ('one can take moral discourse seriously and still admit' its class effects, 1992, p. 216). Carried in the evidence of edges 1 and 3."
