data/extension-2026/canadian-persons-2026-10-14/valverde/entry-draft.json:187:    "evidence_note": "Ruonavaara's abstract describes Corrigan and Sayer's framework as fusing Durkheimian and Foucauldian analysis with basic Marxist theory; Dean's abstract argues that problems in Corrigan's account are better formulated through Foucault's problematic of governmentality. PhD context: 46 of 107 PhDs citing Valverde 1991 also cite Foucault (43% vs 20% of all PhDs). Drawn as a contribution, the atlas's usual kind for Foucault's outgoing edges; an influence edge would need Valverde's own acknowledgement of the debt, which was sought (2026-10-12) but not found in checked text. Not a claim about every Canadian study in the roster.",
